  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd `examples/catalog/2d/adaptive-pocket` with an original U-shaped open pocket.\nInclude the mesh generator, mesh, build script, portable project, NC program, and README.\nRun 2D Adaptive before 2D Pocket with the same 6 mm end mill.\nAdaptive leaves 0.5 mm on the walls and floor.\nPocket removes these allowances and reaches Z6.\nThe README explains the extra corner scallops and material left in sharp corners.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog had no case for Adaptive roughing followed by Pocket finishing.\nThe existing commands already support this sequence.\nNo machining algorithm changes are needed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `adaptive_pocket_case_roughs_above_the_finished_floor_then_finishes`.\n- The pin failed before the case existed. It passes with the case.\n- Mutation: remove the new NC file to restore the upstream absence. The pin fails, then passes after restoration.\n- Mutation: change the Adaptive wall allowance from 0.5 to 0. The pin fails, then passes after restoration.\n- Mutation: change the Adaptive bottom from Z6.5 to Z6. The pin fails, then passes after restoration.\n- Mutation: change the Pocket wall allowance from 0 to 0.5. The pin fails, then passes after restoration.\n- Mutation: change the Pocket bottom from Z6 to Z6.5. The pin fails, then passes after restoration.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: all six cases pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: all five tests pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: all three steps pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passes.\n\nThe new case has no prior file on `upstream/main` to restore with `git show`.\nEach mutation restores the exact original fixture bytes.\nThe pin checks operation types, order, allowances, posted depths, and model portability.\nThe catalog tests regenerate, verify, rebuild from the script, and compare NC bytes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nOne new golden: `examples/catalog/2d/adaptive-pocket/adaptive-pocket.nc`.\nIt contains 13,325 lines for Adaptive roughing to Z6.5 and Pocket finishing to Z6.\nThe diff adds only this case's program. No existing NC or CL golden changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical CNC machine was run.\nBoth operations omit a holder.\nVerification checks for gouges. It does not prove complete stock removal.\nThe cutter leaves material in sharp inside corners.\nPocket recuts the selected region. This case does not demonstrate rest machining.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. The pin uses a new test file and leaves the shared catalog test unchanged.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: Add an open-pocket example with 2D Adaptive roughing and 2D Pocket finishing.\n\nFixes #2860\n",
